=== OBSERVATIONS (backlog, not BL1 failures) ===

O1. No regression test landed. The BL1 manifest contains the template only; the
    four new aria-labelled regions and the two button class strings are guarded
    by NO test in the repo. My mutation-killing probes were throwaway (scratch
    copy only). Recommend the V3 promotion pattern: a test-only follow-up that
    asserts the four regions and the >=24 px classes in rendered output.

O2. axe `empty-table-header` (impact minor, 1 node,
    `<th scope="col" class="w-6"></th>`) fires on /major-expenses at 390 in both
    themes on BOTH master and the branch. Pre-existing, unchanged by BL1, not in
    BL.0's defect table.

O3. Bulk-pin toolbar Apply (50.63 x 21.25) and Clear (47.97 x 21.25) are under
    24 CSS px on branch and master alike. axe passes them (2.5.8 spacing
    exception), so the acceptance criterion is met either way, but if the run
    wants a strict 24 px minimum-size policy these are the remaining two.
    Both readings were judged: the worker's literal reading (leave them) is the
    one the contract's own words support ("text-xs px-2 py-0.5" row action
    buttons; these are toolbar buttons with the utilities in a different order),
    AND it is the one the acceptance oracle (axe) confirms.

O4. Lead brief fact error, no impact on the work: BL.0 attributes the six
    target-size hits to "Restore/Discard and approve/reject". There are no
    approve/reject buttons anywhere in major-expenses.html (grep for
    <button/Approve/Reject enumerates 9 buttons, none of them approve/reject).
    The six are 3x Restore + 3x Discard — this data has three deleted
    definitions. The worker's two source-level edits therefore cover all six
    rendered buttons, which the master-vs-branch axe run confirms (6 -> 0).

O5. The pre-existing anomalous-amount region's label is
    "Matched but anomalous amount table", not the contract's illustrative
    "Exceptions". The four new labels are distinct from it and from each other;
    the two Unmatched labels sit on mutually exclusive template branches so at
    most four regions can ever co-exist.

O6. Harness gap disclosed: the 57 `aria-label="Unpin transaction"` buttons never
    became visible in my probe (0 x 0 even after clicking .major-expense-row-toggle),
    so their target size is unmeasured. The axe applicable-node arithmetic
    (master 418 pass + 6 violations = 424 = branch 424 pass) shows BL1 neither
    added nor removed any target-size-applicable element, so this gap cannot
    hide a BL1-introduced regression.
